.TH CONTROLCENTER\-PROTOCOL 7 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-controlcenter 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
controlcenter-protocol \- newline-delimited JSON status protocol of the Control Center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
TCP 127.0.0.1:9876   (default; \fBCRS_PORT_CMD\fR or \fBstatus_server.port\fR)
request:   <json-object> "\en"
response:  <json-object> "\en"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR controlcenter (1)
runs a TCP server on a daemon thread
.RI ( src/status_server.py ).
Each request is one JSON object on one line; each response is one JSON
object on one line.  A connection may carry many request/response pairs
and is closed by the client.
.PP
This is the only programmatic interface the package exposes.  It is how
other DAQ components push state into the control-room wall display:
the Control Center never polls them, so every indicator is driven by
whatever process chooses to send
.BR set_status .
.SS Wire format
The server buffers until it sees a newline, then decodes one object
.RI ( status_server.py :108-114).
Input that is not valid UTF-8 JSON gets
.PP
.nf
  {"status": "error", "message": "Invalid JSON: <detail>"}
.fi
.PP
and the connection stays open.  A client that never sends a newline is
disconnected after the 30-second read timeout.
.PP
Note the asymmetry between the wire and the CLI: commands on the wire
use underscores
.RB ( set_status ),
while
.BR controlcenter-send (1)
takes hyphens
.RB ( set-status )
and translates.  Hand-written clients must use the underscore form.
.SS Commands
.TP
.B {"command": "ping"}
Answered
.B {"status": "pong"}
directly by the server thread, without involving the GUI
.RI ( status_server.py :120).
It therefore proves the socket and the thread are alive but does
.I not
prove the Qt event loop is still running; a wedged GUI still answers
.BR ping .
.TP
.B {"command": "set_status", "indicator": \fIname\fB, "state": \fIstate\fB, "message": \fItext\fB}
Set one named indicator.
.I state
is one of
.BR ok ", " warning ", " error ", " unknown .
.I message
is optional.
.I name
must match an indicator declared in
.B status_indicators
in the config file; an unknown name is accepted with
.B {"status": "ok"}
but updates nothing, because the call is dispatched to the GUI thread
asynchronously and its result is never collected
.RI ( main_window.py :316-328).
An invalid
.I state
is coerced to
.B unknown
by the widget rather than rejected.
.TP
.B {"command": "set_message", "level": \fIlevel\fB, "text": \fItext\fB}
Show the banner.
.I level
is
.BR info ", " warning ", or " error .
.TP
.B {"command": "clear_message"}
Clear the banner.
.TP
.B {"command": "reload_all"}
Reload every embedded page.  Used after a dashboard behind one of the
cells has been restarted.
.TP
.B {"command": "get_status"}
Return every indicator and its current state:
.PP
.nf
  {"status": "ok", "indicators": {"DAQ": "ok", "Trigger": "warning"}}
.fi
.PP
This is the only command that reads GUI state synchronously from the
server thread rather than posting to the GUI thread.
.SS Responses
.TP
.B {"status": "ok"}
Accepted.  For the four mutating commands this means "queued for the
GUI thread", not "applied".
.TP
.B {"status": "pong"}
Reply to
.BR ping .
.TP
.B {"status": "error", "message": \fItext\fB}
Malformed JSON, an unknown command, or an exception raised by the
handler.
.SH SECURITY
There is no authentication, no authorization and no transport
security.  Any process that can open the port can change what the
control room sees, including clearing an error banner.
.PP
The shipped default binds 127.0.0.1
.RI ( config/controlcenter.yaml :47),
which limits that to local processes.  The bind address is
configurable, and setting
.B status_server.host
to
.BR "" ", " :: ,
or a routable address exposes the port to the network with no
counter-measure.
.B CRS_PORT_CMD
overrides only the port, never the host, so the control-room launch
path cannot accidentally widen the bind.
.SH EXAMPLES
With the shipped client:
.PP
.nf
  controlcenter-send set-status DAQ ok "All systems nominal"
  controlcenter-send get-status
.fi
.PP
Raw, with
.BR nc (1)
\(em note the underscore:
.PP
.nf
  printf '{"command":"set_status","indicator":"DAQ","state":"error"}\en' \e
      | nc 127.0.0.1 9876
.fi
.PP
From Python:
.PP
.nf
  import json, socket
  s = socket.create_connection(("127.0.0.1", 9876), timeout=5)
  s.sendall(json.dumps({"command": "get_status"}).encode() + b"\en")
  print(s.makefile().readline())
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR controlcenter (1),
.BR controlcenter-send (1)
